{
  "comment": "The Common Agent Specification 0.37.0-draft, Section 7.9: an act an agent drafts and its owner approves. Each case is one act. Where form is member, the act is a JSON object whose own specification signs its tag, one newline, and the JCS of the object with the member at sig_at removed, and nothing is removed where the owner's signature is carried beside the object as owner_sig. The marker is the member at marker_at. The draft bytes are those signed bytes computed with the marker removed as well. Where form is beside, the act is a statement with no members, the owner signs the statement's bytes, the marker travels beside it, and the draft bytes are the statement in full. The marker carries exactly agent, draft, drafted_at and sig. draft is sha256: and the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the draft bytes. sig is the drafting agent's Ed25519 signature, in canonical padded base64, over the draft statement: common-agent-draft-v1, one newline, and the JCS of the marker with sig removed. Where the act states a signing instant (signed_at at the top level, or the member at signed_at_at), drafted_at is no later than it. An act is valid when the draft digest matches, the agent's signature verifies, drafted_at is in order, and the owner's signature by owner_key verifies over the act's signed bytes with the marker in place. A marker that fails refuses the whole act. The keys are published test seeds, each the SHA-256 of its label. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: change it only with a spec change alongside.",
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "The Common Agent Specification 0.37.0-draft: 7.9, with Agent SoW 6.3, Agent RFP 6, Agent NDA 7.3 and Agent Reputations 6.1",
